==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:-<ety:bor<fro:-<ety:der<la-lat:prōtēctiō>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|-}}, from {{der|en|fro|-}}, from stem of {{der|en|la-lat|prōtectiō|t=a covering over}}, from {{der|en|la|prōtēctus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|protego|prōtegere|to protect, cover in front}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|ġesċildnes}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|protect|ion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈtɛkʃn̩/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-protection.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|pro|tec|tion}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkʃən|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[process]] of keeping (something or someone) [[safe]].
#: {{ux|en|Raincoats give '''protection''' from rain.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=But then I had the flintlock by me for '''protection'''. ¶ There were giants in the days when that gun was made; for surely no modern mortal could have held that mass of metal steady to his shoulder. The linen-press and a chest on the top of it formed, however, a very good gun-carriage; and, thus mounted, aim could be taken out of the window{{nb...}}.}}
# The state of being safe.
# A means of keeping or remaining safe.
# A means, such as a [[condom]], of preventing pregnancy or sexually transmitted disease.
# {{lb|en|insurance}} [[coverage|Coverage]].
# Immunity from harm, obtained by illegal payments, as bribery or extortion.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[document]] serving as a [[guarantee]] against harm or interference; a [[passport]].
# {{lb|en|economics}} Restrictions on foreign competitors which limit their ability to compete with domestic producers of goods or services.
# {{lb|en|computing}} An instance of a security token associated with a resource (such as a file).
# {{lb|en|euphemism|rare}} {{synonym of|en|adult protection||adult [[incontinence]] [[wear]]}}.

